3. RESTRICTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Except as expressly permitted in Section 2, You SHALL NOT, directly or
indirectly:

3.1 No Source Code Redistribution
    Redistribute, publish, host publicly, mirror, share, sell, lease, or
    sublicense the Engine source code or Your Modifications (in source or
    intermediate form) to any third party.
    (Note: Submitting pull requests or patches directly to Licensor's official
    repository does not violate this section, subject to Licensor's
    contribution terms.)

3.2 No Editor, SDK, or Standalone Engine Redistribution
    Redistribute, publish, sell, or bundle MorbiEditor, the Editor Frontend,
    SDK headers, source templates, or any standalone Engine package, whether
    modified or unmodified.

3.3 No Unrelated Development Tool or Dependency Redistribution
    Redistribute Engine Development Tools or development-time dependencies
    separately from, or in any manner unrelated to, executing a legitimate
    Game Build.

3.4 No Standalone Runtime or Competing Engine Products
    Use the runtime distribution permission in Section 2.4 to:
    (a) distribute Engine Runtime Components on a standalone basis or as a
        reusable library, SDK, plugin, or runtime package for third-party
        developers;
    (b) create, market, or distribute a competing or derivative game engine,
        graphics engine, game editor, authoring suite, middleware, or
        application framework; or
    (c) expose the Engine or Engine Development Tools as a hosted cloud
        development service or engine-as-a-service to third parties.

3.5 No OSI Open-Source Misrepresentation
    Describe, represent, or market this License or the Engine as "OSI-approved
    open source" or under any license other than MESAL v1.0.

3.6 No Removal of Notices
    Remove, obscure, or alter any copyright, license, or third-party
    attribution notices included in the Engine or docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. LEGAL DISTINCTION BETWEEN GAME BUILD DISTRIBUTION AND ENGINE DISTRIBUTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

For the avoidance of doubt, this License establishes a strict legal separation
between:

  (A) GAME BUILD DISTRIBUTION (PERMITTED): Shipping a compiled, end-user Game
      Build (free or commercial) that bundles only the compiled Engine Runtime
      Components required to run that specific Game.

  (B) ENGINE DISTRIBUTION (PROHIBITED): Distributing the Engine itself, its
      source code, Modifications, MorbiEditor, Engine Development Tools, SDKs,
      headers, or standalone Engine Runtime Components outside of an end-user
      Game Build.

Permission to perform (A) never implies, expands into, or grants permission to
perform (B).

